+## Automatic Runs (opt-in)
+
+For a DAG the user wants advanced without supervision, create an automatic Run
+instead of dispatching every step yourself:
+
+```text
+ORCA orchestration run-create --objective "<goal>" --mode automatic --max-parallel 2 --json
+ORCA orchestration workflow-apply --run <run_id> --workflow-file <path|-> --expected-version 0 --json
+ORCA orchestration run-start --id <run_id> --json
+```
+
+The runtime executor launches ready Tasks itself; normal starts and completions do
+not wake you and never call a model. Work only when woken:
+
+- A decision gate (review, failure, ambiguity) arrives: read `check`, resolve it
+  with `gate-resolve --id <gate> --resolution approved|changes_requested` (or your
+  answer), and end your turn.
+- A final report arrives once the Run settles: summarize outcomes and evidence.
+- `run-pause` stops new launches; running workers continue. `run-resume`
+  re-evaluates ready Tasks. `run-cancel` blocks new launches and requests guarded
+  stops; an unproven stop stays visible as cancelling/stop_unknown.
+
+Do not poll, watch, or run `check` to drive progress. Do not manually start a Task
+in an automatic Run unless the user asks; manual starts share its pause, capacity
+and decision-gate rules. A workflow may include explicit `review`/`correction`
+Tasks; correction work is capped at two rounds.
+
